{#
The heading row of a collapsible sidebar section — LABELS and ACCOUNTS — as
the <summary> of the section's <details class="group/section">.

One template, embedded by both, so the two headings are the same HTML and
cannot drift apart. They had: two hand-kept copies, and the ACCOUNTS one,
with a second button in it, ran out of room first as the sidebar was dragged
narrower. Its chevron had no shrink-0, so flexbox squeezed the icon instead
and the heading slid sideways under the drag. Here the chevron keeps its
width, and the actions are small enough that the row fits (see below).

A .nav-item, like every row under it and the More summary above: the same
pill off the sidebar's edge on hover, and the same inline padding, which
puts the chevron exactly where px-3 did. It used to be a rounded-lg box of
its own, a different shape from every row it heads.

  heading    the visible heading, also the summary's accessible name
  collapsed  whether the section is rendered shut

Blocks:
  badge      anything between the heading and the actions (LABELS' roll-up)
  actions    the heading's buttons

Named explicitly (aria-label), because a summary takes its accessible name
from its contents, and these contain a badge and buttons — unnamed, LABELS
read as "Labels 3 unread Create label". The same string as the visible
heading, so a voice user asking for "Labels" still gets this.

The buttons are quiet until the heading row is hovered (`group/head`, the
summary, not the section: a row further down must not light them up). Two
exits from that, both needed: keyboard focus shows a button, or one reached
with Tab would be invisible while it holds focus; and it is only hidden where
there is a hover to reveal it with — `[@media(hover:hover)]` — or a phone
could neither create a label nor add an account. `transition` rather than
`transition-colors`, so the fade is one.

Plain icons, not square buttons: a padded 26px square each was what pushed
the ACCOUNTS heading out of its row as the sidebar narrowed (chevron, word,
two squares and their gaps were 156px of the 140px a 180px sidebar has). The
icons are sized by font size, 11px like the account row's ⋯, because Font
Awesome fixes an icon's width at 1.25em and a w-* class does nothing to it:
13.75px each, and the row fits at the narrowest width, so the heading's
truncate is a guard that does not fire. The ring stands in for
the hover square when a button has keyboard focus.

Callers put `section_action_class` on each button, set here so all of them
are the same control.
#}
{% set section_action_class = 'shrink-0 flex items-center justify-center rounded-sm text-gray-400 hover:text-ink-soft transition cursor-pointer
    focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent
    [@media(hover:hover)]:opacity-0 group-hover/head:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100' %}
<summary class="nav-item group/head py-1 flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer list-none transition-colors hover:bg-hover"
         aria-label="{{ heading }}"
         aria-expanded="{{ collapsed ? 'false' : 'true' }}"
         data-ui--sidebar-target="collapseSummary">
    <i class="fa-solid fa-chevron-right w-3 shrink-0 text-[9px] text-ink-faint transition-transform group-open/section:rotate-90" aria-hidden="true"></i>
    <span class="flex-1 min-w-0 truncate text-xs font-semibold text-ink-faint uppercase tracking-wider">{{ heading }}</span>
    {%- block badge %}{% endblock -%}
    {%- block actions %}{% endblock -%}
</summary>
